## Fixes in the commit

- F601 (lesson-flow.tsx): the end region drops focus:outline-none and holds the two-tone ring
  of the loop panel controls: focus:outline-3 focus:outline-white focus:outline-offset-0
  focus:[box-shadow:0_0_0_6px_var(--st-brown)]. That is the same 3 px ring that look.css gives
  :is(a, button, [tabindex]):focus-visible, which the region matches through its tabIndex=-1.
  The focus move keeps focus({ preventScroll: true }).
- F603 (lesson-flow.tsx, week-view.tsx): min-h-11 on the Thai toggle, the "Back to the week"
  link, and the "Next step" control of the flow, and on the five "Open the lesson" links of
  the week view. No other layout change.
- F605 (week-view.tsx, lesson-flow.tsx): lang="en" on the 16 English text elements of the week
  view (the level line, the seven section headings, the five lesson links, and the three
  material labels) and on the step id chip of the flow. The existing pickLang and noteLangsOf
  helpers already cover every dynamic bilingual field; the named elements are static English,
  so they take the literal mark.
- F495 and F496 (docs/runbooks/storytime-deploy.md, flag section only): the section states
  that the flag stays in the service template after the on command, that every later build
  revision carries it, that a traffic rollback does not remove it, and that the operator reads
  /th/teacher/2/1 on the tag URL before each traffic step and runs the off command to clear
  the template; it sends the operator to sign in as the teacher on the tag URL host first,
  because a session cookie is bound to one host; it adds the env compare of the new revision
  and the live revision (two gcloud run revisions describe lines with
  --format='value(spec.containers[0].env)'); it renames the image placeholder to
  <the live revision image reference with its digest> and says the read value goes into
  --image as it is, a full reference with @sha256:. --no-traffic, the tags, Daniel's go, and
  the way back stay. No gcloud command ran; the runbook is text only.

